title: Migrating from GSD5 to HyperGSD
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

!! What changed

* ''Performance'' is much better with a large number of action tiddlers. You will never have to delete completed actions again!
* A new ''picker'' lets you easily select projects and dependencies which filters options as you type, replacing the select boxes of GSD5.
* Actions may now have ''multiple dependencies and pre-requisites'', up from just one before.
* ''Realms'' have been completely overhauled as a tag-based system (`$:/GSD/Realm/<RealmName>`). The realm selector has also been re-worked, letting you specifically view items //not in any realm// for the first time.
** The warning for when you are looking at another realm is now a globe {{$:/plugins/yan/HyperGSD/images/globe}} and appears across both the panel and lists.
* ''Contexts'', ''contacts'' and ''references'' are now optional sub-plugins.
* ''Ticklers'' are back! Again as an optional sub-plugin.

!!! Picker and list refreshing

To eliminate UI lag during typing and navigation, the filters in the panel dropdowns (Contact, Project, and Pre-requisite) have been stripped of all dynamic variables. This allows TiddlyWiki to aggressively cache them.

* ''Broken links'': If you e.g. assign a contact to an action and then delete that contact tiddler entirely, the dropdown will display as blank (`-- none --`) because the engine no longer performs an expensive fallback search to find the missing title.

!! Pre-requisites

* A working TiddlyWiki with GSD5 data.
* The ''HyperGSD'' plugin installed and the old GSD5 `core` plugin disabled.

!! Mandatory

!!! Migrate fields to tags

# Turn off timestamps (so not to ruin your wiki history): {{$:/core/ui/Buttons/timestamp}}
# Press this button to migrate dependencies from `gsd_action` to `gsd_prerequisites`, which will allow you to track multiple dependencies: <$button>
Copy all "gsd_action" values to "gsd_prerequisites"
<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to copy gsd_action and format it into gsd_prerequisites across ALL tiddlers? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently.">
<$list filter="[has[gsd_action]]">
    <$action-setfield
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $field="gsd_prerequisites"
        $value={{{ [<currentTiddler>get[gsd_action]format:titlelist[]] }}}
    />
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button>
# Filter for all actions (`[gsd_type[action]]`) and bulk add the tag `$:/GSD/Action`: <$button>Tag all actions<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to add the tag $:/GSD/Action to all tiddlers which carry gsd_type: action? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently?">
<$list filter="[gsd_type[action]]">
    <$action-listops
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $tags="+[append[$:/GSD/Action]]"
    />
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button>
# Filter for all projects (`[gsd_type[project]]`) and bulk add the tag `$:/GSD/Project`: <$button>Tag all projects<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to add the tag $:/GSD/Project to all tiddlers which carry gsd_type: project? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently?">
<$list filter="[gsd_type[project]]">
    <$action-listops
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $tags="+[append[$:/GSD/Project]]"
    />
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button>
# Filter for all contacts (`[gsd_type[contact]]`) and bulk add the tag `$:/GSD/Contact`: <$button>Tag all contacts<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to add the tag $:/GSD/Contact to all tiddlers which carry gsd_type: contact? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently?">
<$list filter="[gsd_type[contact]]">
    <$action-listops
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $tags="+[append[$:/GSD/Contact]]"
    />
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button>
# Filter for all references (`[gsd_type[reference]]`) and bulk add the tag `$:/GSD/Reference`: <$button>Tag all references<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to add the tag $:/GSD/Reference to all tiddlers which carry gsd_type: reference? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently?">
<$list filter="[gsd_type[reference]]">
    <$action-listops
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $tags="+[append[$:/GSD/Reference]]"
    />
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button>
# Convert every `gsd_realm` value into a matching `$:/GSD/Realm/<realm-name>` tag: <$button>Copy realms to unique tags
<$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to add the matching $:/GSD/Realm/ tag to every tiddler carrying gsd_realm? Please ensure timestamps are off so your modified dates are not changed inadvertently.">
<$list filter="[has[gsd_realm]]">
    <$let realm-tag-titlelist={{{ [<currentTiddler>get[gsd_realm]addprefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]format:titlelist[]] }}}>
    <$action-listops
        $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
        $tags="+[append<realm-tag-titlelist>]"
    />
    </$let>
</$list>
</$action-confirm>
</$button><br>Migrated realms should appear automatically in the [[capture|$:/plugins/yan/HyperGSD/ui/sidebar/capture-sidebar]] and [[review|$:/plugins/yan/HyperGSD/ui/sidebar/review-sidebar]] sidebars.

''Why:'' Original GSD5 relied entirely on the `gsd_type` field to identify items. HyperGSD relies 100% on specific TiddlyWiki tags to leverage the internal tag index for instantaneous database lookups.



''Why:'' HyperGSD uses tags for higher-performance filtering than fields.

!!! Migrate contexts

# Register your context tags in the [[GSD/Contexts]] dashboard (or just tag with <<tag GSD/Contexts>>.
# Any tiddler carrying that tag will now display its own GSD dashboard when opened.

!! Optional

!!! Migrate ticklers

''Ticklers'' now live in the optional [[HyperGSD Ticklers|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-ticklers/readme]] sub-plugin. GSD5 ticklers were actions carrying `gsd_tickdate` (and optionally `gsd_tickdays`).
The HyperGSD sub-plugin reads the same data from renamed fields:

|GSD5 |HyperGSD |h
|`gsd_tickdate` |`gsd_tickler_date` |
|`gsd_tickdays` |`gsd_tickler_repeat_days` |

GSD5 ticklers were actions, so the "Tag all actions" button above will have already given them the `$:/GSD/Action` tag. An empty or non-existent repeat interval means the tickler triggers only once.

Use this button, which will not update timestamps, to copy the old fields across and delete them:
<$button>
    Migrate tickler fields
    <$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to copy gsd_tickdate/gsd_tickdays to gsd_tickler_date/gsd_tickler_repeat_days and delete the old fields across ALL tiddlers?">
        <$list filter="[all[tiddlers]has[gsd_tickdate]]">
            <$action-setfield
                $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
                $timestamp="no"
                gsd_tickler_date={{!!gsd_tickdate}}
                gsd_tickler_repeat_days={{!!gsd_tickdays}}
            />
            <$action-deletefield
                $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
                $timestamp="no"
                gsd_tickdate
                gsd_tickdays
            />
        </$list>
    </$action-confirm>
</$button>

''Why:'' the sub-plugin keys off `gsd_tickler_date` on tagged actions; the rename keeps your due dates and repeat intervals intact. If you would rather not use ticklers, skip this section — the old fields are inert without the sub-plugin.

!!! Clean up redundant fields

You can delete the following fields from all tiddlers:

* `gsd_type`
* `gsd_realm`
* `gsd_context`
* `gsd_action`
* `gsd_perserve` -- a typo carried over from old GSD5 versions, serving no functional purpose

Use this button, which will not update timestamps:
<$button>
    Delete GSD Fields
    <$action-confirm $message="Are you sure you want to delete the old GSD5 fields from all tiddlers?">
        <$list filter="[has[gsd_type]] [has[gsd_realm]] [has[gsd_context]] [has[gsd_action]] [has[gsd_perserve]]">
            <$action-deletefield
                $tiddler=<<currentTiddler>>
                $timestamp="no"
                gsd_type
                gsd_realm
                gsd_context
                gsd_action
                gsd_perserve
            />
        </$list>
    </$action-confirm>
</$button>

''Why:'' HyperGSD relies entirely on tags for identity and categorisation, making these legacy fields completely redundant. Removing them reduces tiddler weight and keeps the database clean.

!!! Update dashboard titles

* Rename your primary dashboards (e.g. rename `Action Dashboard` to `GSD/Action Dashboard`).
* Ensure your sidebar links or any custom shortcuts are updated to point to the new `GSD/` prefixed titles.

''Why:'' To keep the main tiddler list clean, HyperGSD has all built-in dashboards prefixed with `GSD/`.